						 <p>every time I close my eyes I see the banana man. he places his hand on my shoulder. I shift in my discomfort. he stares into my soul. I blush. he asks me if I want a sprite cranberry, and I politely decline. he asks again. I decline. he asks again with a new insistence. I try to pull away. his grip tightens, and I pull harder. he clamps down, and I find myself unable to move. with a loud, booming voice, he asks again. DO YOU WANT A SPRITE CRANBERRY? I say no again. he forces me to the ground and opens my mouth. I scream. he tells me there is no use in resistance. he drowns me with a sprite cranberry.</p> <p>+1</p> 
